     #1E8449 is the access dot for «images, free, no account», and it is the
     obvious colour to reach for — but measured it is 3.66:1 on the paper
     ground and 3.46:1 on the dark card, which is large-text territory and
     this glyph is 13px. So the dot's green stays a dot, and the pill takes
     the nearest value that actually clears 4.5:1 on both halves of the site:
     #176B3A on paper (5.10) and #4FB477 on the dark card (6.32).
     Three blocks, the same three the token file uses and for the same reason
     — the system default, the OS preference scoped so an explicit light
     choice still wins, and the explicit dark choice. */
  /* THREE STATES, THREE TONES. Nothing recorded is quiet — it is the resting
     state of most rows on most visits and must not shout. Started is --brass,
     which is this project's own amber and the one colour here that has been
